# If you control but don't own Old-Growth Troll, you (not its owner) return it when it dies, enchanting a Forest you control
# (the rulings: it returns under the control of the ability's controller, CR 603.3a). Bot2 owns the Troll and no Forest. Bot1 steals it with Act
# of Treason and destroys it with Infernal Grasp: it returns under Bot1's control on Bot1's Forest, and Bot2 owns the card.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Act of Treason
Infernal Grasp
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Old-Growth Troll
Plains x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: G)
Bot2.Hand.Old-Growth Troll.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Act of Treason.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Old-Growth Troll)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Infernal Grasp.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Old-Growth Troll)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Old-Growth Troll.AttachedTo = Forest
Bot1.Battlefield.Old-Growth Troll.Types = Enchantment
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
